A = \left[ {\matrix{ {\cos \theta } & {\sin \theta }  \cr { - \sin \theta } & {\cos \theta }  \cr

} } \right] 

$A^{2}$ =  \left[ {\matrix{ {\cos \theta } & {\sin \theta }  \cr { - \sin \theta } & {\cos \theta }  \cr

} } \right]  \left[ {\matrix{ {\cos \theta } & {\sin \theta }  \cr { - \sin \theta } & {\cos \theta }  \cr

} } \right] 

$\Rightarrow A^{2}$ =  \left[ {\matrix{ {\cos 2\theta } & {\sin 2\theta }  \cr { - \sin 2\theta } & {\cos 2\theta }  \cr

} } \right] 

Similarly, $A^{n}$ =  \left[ {\matrix{ {\cos n\theta } & {\sin n\theta }  \cr { - \sin n\theta } & {\cos n\theta }  \cr

} } \right] 

$\therefore$ B = A + $A^{4}$

=  \left[ {\matrix{ {\cos \theta } & {\sin \theta }  \cr { - \sin \theta } & {\cos \theta }  \cr

} } \right]  +  \left[ {\matrix{ {\cos 4\theta } & {\sin 4\theta }  \cr { - \sin 4\theta } & {\cos 4\theta }  \cr

} } \right] 

=  \left[ {\matrix{ {\cos 4\theta  + \cos \theta } & {\sin 4\theta  + \sin \theta }  \cr { - \sin 4\theta  - \sin \theta } & {\cos 4\theta  + \cos \theta }  \cr

} } \right] 

detB = (cos4$\theta$ + cos$\theta$)^{2} + (sin4$\theta$ + sin$\theta$)^{2}

